WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:03.440
Beginning final check of internal <i>Kivotos</i> systems.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.480
Communication network.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.360
Electricity generation.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.190
Propulsion.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.730
All systems are green.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.740
Transferring control authority to <i>Kivotos</i>.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.490
Boost capacitor has met engine ignition requirements.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.660
Thruster engine now idling.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:21.450
<i>Kivotos</i> hangar entrance is now ninety-three percent open.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:26.920
Releasing docking bolts A0 to F10.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.420
<i>Kivotos</i> thruster ignition confirmed.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.380
Output is rising.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.720
Guidance beacon signal response is nominal.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.850
<i>Kivotos</i> following specified coordinates.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.810
The <i>Kivotos</i> was designed to function as an independent spaceship,

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:46.560
but it only has standard rocket propulsion.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:51.480
But theoretically, it's possible for it to undergo hyperspace transport

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.660
while it's docked with the <i>Blume</i> via Entangle Link.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.030
This will be our first time actually doing it, though.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.910
This is risky...

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.620
Navigation system.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.170
Autopilot.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.040
Directional transmitter system.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:09.790
Check.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.050
Avionics okay.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:19.100
This will be the first time someone from Earth has experienced an Entangle Link.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:24.390
We can't predict what effect it will have on our human crew members.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:27.100
There's no previous data to guide us.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:30.690
But the captain and Akari will be fine.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:33.190
That is what I think.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.160
Is that your intuition?

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.280
Yes.

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.410
I'll trust it.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.250
Come to think of it,

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.710
what happened to that thing they were developing on the lunar base?

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.550
You really do know everything.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.050
Lunar base?

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.680
The Planter Unit.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.550
Planter Unit?

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.680
Originally, Hana was the one at greatest risk with the ark plan.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:15.030
Hana couldn't leave the <i>Blume</i> on her own.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:20.280
The ark plan would try to force the <i>Blume</i> to move

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.120
without regard for her safety.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.160
I didn't like that.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.330
That risk is still here.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.800
Anyway, the lunar base was developing something called a Planter Unit.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.670
The idea was that Hana's brain wave resonance

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.260
and bioinformatics could be digitally applied to the <i>Blume</i> there

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:45.350
because of the moon's low ambient brain wave resonance,

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:48.310
and in doing so control it remotely.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:54.320
Commander Nishikubo was in charge of the project. That way, if it became necessary

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:58.990
to use the <i>Blume</i>, we could minimize the risk to Hana.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.160
I'm fine.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.870
I've got the captain.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.590
Then what's the Planter Unit's status?

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:18.550
Only Commander Nishikubo would know.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:23.390
But if there was even a one-percent chance that it would work,

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.640
he would have told you about it.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.520
Yeah,

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.730
I guess you're right.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.280
Pointer screwed up.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.650
Yes, he screwed up.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:44.450
The future of the chosen boys,

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.740
humanity's hope for survival,

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.910
is being cut off by the Intercept Faction.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.210
That's how it seems to me.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:56.750
But the cold sleep block is still aboard the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:01.670
Rewinding the clock to the ark plan is still an option.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.130
There's still time.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:07.760
But they will launch the <i>Blume</i> soon.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.430
We cannot let that happen.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.230
It is we who will use the <i>Blume</i>.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.440
It shouldn't matter if it gets a bit banged up first.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.320
We must retake it, no matter what.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:27.370
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:34.540
I'm watching an endless dream

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:41.010
Aren't you watching too?

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:48.350
It's always close by no matter how far away it seems

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:55.190
Can't you see it too?

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:00.610
The things you can't normally say

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.360
The things you try to express

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.860
The things you're willing to fight for

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:11.580
Standing on your own two feet

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:18.250
The night sky illuminates them all

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:25.380
The first flash of lightning

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:31.720
This is our battle to fight

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:39.060
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:47.530
This dream will absolutely come true

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.950
Eternal life...

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:58.370
If I really had such a thing, what would I do?

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:02.550
It is truly a hard question for a snob like myself to contemplate.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:07.220
For example, whatever it is you enjoy most today,

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.390
like that delicious wine...

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:13.310
What must you do to enjoy it forever?

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:19.770
Or how to enjoy time with beautiful ladies.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:22.570
I think that is what I would think of.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:25.990
To consider it a bit more realistically,

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:29.320
in my case, if I were to live for eternity...

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:33.530
I might be a little irritated by the size of the world I have to live in,

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:38.290
and the fact that there are still so many things I do not know.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.370
Yes.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.580
First, I'd be irritated.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:46.170
This may not be the answer you're looking for. Please forgive me.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.590
Pac does not lie.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.890
Ah, I got that wrong.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:58.430
As Kube Masaki, send that as my answer to Peter Westvillage.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.900
Understood.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:04.360
Amarok and the others' full-scale attack...

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.440
...is about...

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:09.450
Begin
The Operation
Summer

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.280
...to begin.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.950
Now, let's get started.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:18.290
Bagbear and Lady Setsuna will soon return with the final capsule.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:19.910
It's nearly time.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.670
Earth's last night.

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.880
It's the end of the world, huh?

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.990
This planet wasn't that bad.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:55.030
Nor was this avatar body.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:01.540
That crêpe truck we ran together was pretty fun, wasn't it?

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.500
What are you talking about?

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:12.130
He'd feel irritated first, huh?

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.810
Commander.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:22.770
We've made contact with both the <i>Kivotos</i> and the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:29.690
Commander, we heard about the Planter Unit.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.150
Akari again?

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:37.120
That isn't even close to complete.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.700
The research team did their best, but...

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:41.620
I'm sorry.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.710
Thanks, though.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:49.170
I heard that you made it because you were concerned about me.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.840
You can be pretty nice sometimes!

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:56.220
G-Governor Yomatsuri!

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:58.300
But it's true.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:02.350
DEFCON 1?

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.640
Everyone, this is an emergency.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.150
Over the last 120 seconds,

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:12.070
the mass incidence of coma victims we last witnessed in Tokyo

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:15.110
has reoccurred in no less than 25 places.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.820
We should assume that the Planetary Gears

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:23.660
have been gathering high-density libido on a scale unseen up to this point.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:27.250
According to a report that's just come in,

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:35.170
Alonzo's predictive simulations suggest there's a 99.98% chance that all the

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:40.810
Planetary Gears on Earth will launch a full-scale attack in Kill-T-Gang form.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:44.810
99.98%?

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.890
A full-scale attack?

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:50.360
Seven Kill-T-Gangs all attacking at once?

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:54.110
And it could happen right now?

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:55.780
Commander.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.570
I understand there's no time to waste.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:06.750
The Midsummer's Knights will now launch their attack on enemy mother ship <i>Oberon</i>,

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.250
the fortress-class carrier in orbit around Uranus.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.390
Protect our Earth.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.050
Roger.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:24.520
They can do this, right?

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:25.520
Yeah.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:28.730
Let's go swimming again, Teppei!

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:30.400
Roger.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:31.940
We'll be back, Governor.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.980
Hana!

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.700
We'll be back, Mom!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:46.700
I'll be waiting.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:48.580
Teppei,

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.830
take care of Akari.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:52.380
Right.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:57.380
Wipe them out, and come back safely.

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.260
Those are the terms of success for this mission.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:00.800
Got it?

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:01.720
Roger!

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:03.600
Daichi?

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.890
The anniversary of Taiyo's death is in a week.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:10.440
Let's go visit his grave together.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:14.860
Right!

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:16.530
For sure.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:19.490
It's a promise.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.370
This is the team we hoped for.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:27.120
That's what I think.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.790
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:35.250
Everyone, you heard the situation.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.010
At this very moment,

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:43.930
the enemy might launch an attack with seven Kill-T-Gangs.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:49.600
Our ship, the <i>Blume</i>, will head directly for the mother ship <i>Oberon</i>,

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.020
the fortress-class carrier in orbit around Uranus.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.810
If I concentrate on the Entangle Link,

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:59.110
I can't use the <i>Blume</i>'s normal weapons or change our course at all.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:00.650
Don't worry.

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:02.450
We'll protect you.

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:05.160
Leave it to us.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:09.450
Okay.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.540
I'm going to the <i>Blume</i>.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.380
Hana, are you sure about this?

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:23.550
Captain?

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.300
When this mission is over,

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:32.140
let's go to a festival and eat a candy apple together!

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:35.270
Hana?

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:39.150
Captain...

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:48.490
When you destroyed that debris back there,

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.950
my only thought was that at last, you'd truly become the Captain.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:57.670
Keep it to remind yourself of that.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.090
I'll be a real captain

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:04.720
when this mission is successfully completed.

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.300
Until then, keep it for me.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:09.560
Got it.

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:18.690
Hana, can you hear me?

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:20.400
I can hear you.

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:24.530
Can you use your Livlaster?

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:26.240
I can.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:32.120
I'm starting up the main engine.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:35.330
Okay, I'll let you handle the timing.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:39.130
Let's save the Earth together, partner.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:42.840
Yeah. Leave it to me, partner!

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:58.230
Looks like they're attacking with the <i>Blume</i>, after all.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:01.730
They have the <i>Blume</i> and the Livlaster.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:05.150
Ai's failure with that debris plan hurt us a lot.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:05.940
What?

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.530
It's all my fault?

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:13.990
Does Albion really intend to destroy the Cocoon and all of our Ego Blocks?

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.620
I don't really know.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:22.090
Does he intend to die here, in this solar system?

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:28.430
If the Cocoon is destroyed, we won't be able to leave

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.590
after consuming all the Earthlings' libido energy.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:35.680
But it looks like they've sent the whole gang.

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:38.060
Manatsu Daichi and Yomatsuri Akari, too?

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:45.030
If their minds survive the Entangle Link, it might just be possible that they'd take them.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:49.990
Well, having a Neoteny around would be helpful.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:56.830
I can't imagine an Earthling being able to withstand an Entangle Link's hyperspace transport.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:01.250
Their weak minds are pitiful.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.340
Their arrogance knows no bounds.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.300
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:09.510
This will be an interesting distraction before our attack.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.890
An Impactor has appeared in front of the <i>Blume</i>.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:20.480
Omega sector.

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:21.480
Distance: 150,000.

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:23.190
An Impactor?

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:25.820
The Garm Engine...

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:32.280
A massive Impactor developed by the Ark Faction to capture the Kill-T-Gangs.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:34.620
It must be Salty Dog.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:36.660
At a time like this?

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.870
Didn't we tell you we'd protect you?

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.420
You concentrate on the Entangle Link.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:45.590
Roger.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.250
Teppei, Akari...

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.170
Let's go.

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:49.010
Roger.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:52.430
We will now begin Operation Summer.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:26.630
In terms of size, that monster's as big as the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:29.460
It's entering our firing range, Captain.

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:34.050
Mid-sized Impactors are splitting off from the Garm Engine!

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:37.010
It's Cerberus!

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:38.220
Cerberus?

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:42.810
I'll head out in the Earth.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.440
Take care of the ship, Teppei.

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:45.900
You understand, don't you, Captain?

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:52.070
If something happens to you, Hana won't be able to leave the <i>Blume</i>.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.860
Yeah, I know.

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:10.960
A beam cannon?

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:43.750
The Earth Engine has left the ship and engaged Cerberus.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.960
It's leaving the <i>Blume</i> behind.

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:49.040
The <i>Blume</i> has engaged the Garm Engine.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.850
That's the Livlaster DC's barrier.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:06.310
Wow.

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.230
He can use it from the <i>Kivotos</i>.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:24.410
I guess we can't damage it from long range.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:28.750
It'll hurt us, not being able to use the <i>Blume</i>'s weapons...

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:30.380
What do we do?

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:46.180
Form a strong image in your mind of the place you want to go.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:13.710
I can see it.

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:30.980
Akari,

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:32.730
it's connected.

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:34.400
We can jump soon.

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:35.570
Roger.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:37.190
Captain, you heard that, right?

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:41.990
The Entangle Link will begin soon!

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:42.860
Hurry!

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.160
That stupid kid thinks he's a hero.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:55.790
Don't interfere with our plan to save humanity!

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:02.630
Why are you interfering?

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:10.600
This mission is

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:13.060
to save Earth!

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.870
We're entering the Entangle Link?

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:32.410
But the captain isn't back yet.

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:33.580
No...

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:34.370
Hana?

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:37.340
I can't stop...

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:40.460
I can't control it anymore!

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:43.680
Captain, hurry!

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:52.100
Don't let them escape, Garm!

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:14.870
Hana...

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:19.710
When this mission is over,

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:24.470
let's go to a festival and eat a candy apple together!

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:27.840
Yeah,

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:28.800
it's a promise!

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:47.490
Get there!

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:57.830
Oh, no!

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:00.210
I can't dodge it!

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:28.450
Daichi?

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:30.120
Time to get up.

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:32.580
Okay...

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:42.040
A dream?

00:24:12.720 --> 00:24:14.430
I woke up to find myself in my room.

00:24:15.050 --> 00:24:16.390
I'm Manatsu Daichi,

00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:17.970
a second-year high school student.

00:24:17.970 --> 00:24:19.720
And summer break starts tomorrow.

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:21.270
A normal, everyday life.

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:23.020
But why?

00:24:23.730 --> 00:24:27.070
The wind in this town feels wrong, somehow...

00:24:27.520 --> 00:24:31.110
And I keep thinking about the dream I had last night,

00:24:31.110 --> 00:24:32.740
but I can't remember it.

00:24:33.070 --> 00:24:36.120
Next time, on episode 23 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:36.120 --> 00:24:38.200
A Midsummer Night's Dream

00:24:36.570 --> 00:24:38.200
A Midsummer Night's Dream.

00:24:38.490 --> 00:24:42.040
Earth Engine... What's that, again?
